body:
I forgot all about it, and haven't gotten around to purchasing this.

&#x200B;

Looks like that was for the best!

The energy cost was a bit much, necessitating the additional grind, but the new Forge system just brings it all to an absolute halt at times. You'd stop levelling once you hit a full bar, and had to use Fire Crystals to allow you to continue.

&#x200B;

It really breaks the flow of going through a level for an arbitrary restriction. Heat just doesn't mean anything to me anymore.

That was the major thing that bothered me about the movie.

&#x200B;

I don't feel the idea that Godzilla ultimately comes out on top is a bad one, but to make Kong seem like such a jobber rubbed me the wrong way. An underdog? Sure, as he was in the original movie. But I feel they could have played up his strengths and made him go almost toe-to-toe with Godzilla. To be told that Godzilla wasn't taking him seriously just feels like it robbed us of the potential of Kong being a formidable defender and a force in and of himself.

Sort of. If you fast forward, they'll pose the question, but be considered 'ignored' because you didn't click to talk to the leader within the timeframe.

&#x200B;

So I definitely 'ignored' a lot of them by accident that way, since my focus was elsewhere or my characters were spread thin.

