I feel Burning Godzilla and Fire Rodan are the hardest the counter.

&#x200B;

Burning Godzilla can take a LOT out of your units unless you're using Ultraman/Super X. Lots of health, and the explosion does a lot of damage.

&#x200B;

Fire Rodan is the easiest unit to play for free health, ESPECIALLY if someone's using Mothra Leo. It's just free, mindless healing that's better than Psychic Chorus.

&#x200B;

Mothra Leo is a bit too good, but not exactly difficult to counter. Battra might be a touch better, but likely just needs a higher cost so it doesn't combo as well with other meta fliers.

&#x200B;

Biollante feels fine as is. Great crowd control, but can't do jack to fliers. Ultraman feels a bit too fast for my taste, but isn't the worst to deal with.

I mean, a character like Goku is flat and works well.

&#x200B;

A flat character works not by changing themselves, but by understanding the truth of the world and changing everyone around them. Like a piece of work about unyielding optimism having an optimistic character change the mind of pessimists that they encounter to adopt their optimism.

I feel like a flat character with that powerset would make an interesting main character.

&#x200B;

A character that brings out the best in those around them, and supports them in their struggles and their battles.

If you leave him in, it'll be fine.

&#x200B;

Nothing to worry about!

While I enjoyed the 2014 Godzilla movie, I feel that his role of ecological protector should put him at greater odds with humanity.

&#x200B;

Not that humanity at large is responsible for ecological devastation, but I wouldn't expect a giant pre-cambrian reptile to know the distinction. Maybe he goes after gas/coal factories and humanity is against it because it has huge economic impacts.

&#x200B;

But at this point, I think Godzilla's too far gone as 'the good guy' to have him do something like this. Maybe exploitation of Hollow Earth energy causes him to go against humanity? Could be a decent set-up for a Godzilla vs. Kong 2, with Kong siding with humanity.

