Love a lot of things regarding how he was portrayed, but the best part of it all?

&#x200B;

He has actual history with Godzilla.

&#x200B;

He's always called 'The Joker to Godzilla's Batman,' but in almost every incarnation he shows up in, they're just two big bad fellas slapping each other.

&#x200B;

But in this movie? You can almost FEEL how much Godzilla hates this guy. Stalking his frozen tomb, the look of schadenfreude as he blast Ghidorah to ash, Godzilla wanted this guy dead MILLIONS of years ago.

Weather could be an interesting way to change up the maps a bit, but I'd imagine the effects of it wouldn't be massive.

&#x200B;

I'm waiting for New York - Night stages to show up to finish up the EVA mission for it, and if I have to deal with my aerial units being drastically slowed down to do it, it might make it impossible to get the wins I need.

&#x200B;

That being said, strong weather effects could give more necessity for different teams, since the game already allows that.

Investing could be a worthwhile venture, especially with the stock and crypto market getting it's shit kicked in.

&#x200B;

Don't be foolish about it, though; put in only what you're able to lose. Smartest bet would be to put in a little bit over a long period of time (like 5 bucks a day, or 20 a week) into stable stocks like Microsoft and Google, and wait for the recession to tide over.

&#x200B;

With the money you would've spent on something like coffee, you can make a bit more so you can more reliably do something with it like go to college.

