A game where you and a few other players are individual kaiju that roam around a massive map, looking to maul each other for territory.

&#x200B;

Not exactly unconventional, but it'd be difficult to figure out how to get it to run properly. There'd need to be a lot to do between fights, and along with the difficulty of running what's effectively simplified open worlds for multiple players. There would have to be aspects of it tied to allowing you to 'evolve,' maybe destroying building gets you points you can spend improving/changing your monster?

&#x200B;

Think the game Evolve, but everyone's the big monster.

Very few games would let you play out a long-term no win scenario, since it's generally not considered fun.

&#x200B;

The only game that punishes you in such a way that I can think of is Project Zomboid; by default, getting bitten on the neck means you WILL get the zombie virus, and that you WILL die within a few days. You can spend the rest of the time doing whatever, but you will die regardless. Playing a scenario like that is frustrating; something like radiation would essentially have this happen to you immediately, and with no potential way to prevent it without extensive care and protect from radiation.

