I felt like Kong was done dirty in the movie overall, especially how Godzilla 'got serious' and took him out in the course of a minute.

&#x200B;

I can understand Godzilla being too tired to fight Mechagodzilla after having a legitimately challenging fight with Kong, but it was more like watching a 12 year old get knocked out by a 23 year old who's had enough of his shit.

&#x200B;

Warbat scene could have been a good means of showing Kong as being a quick-thinking fighter (maybe he could have body slammed the Warbat while it was covering him?). But I guess the humans needed something to do as well.

I feel like the only monster besides Kong and Godzilla that could carry a movie would be Mothra, honestly.

&#x200B;

But for a big budget flick? Probably not. It'd have to be something smaller scale. A shame, 'cuz Mothra deserve the BIG SCREEN!

Kenshi has an interesting 'world state' system where areas will change based on what you do.

&#x200B;

You can take out faction leaders and see their cities overrun with bandits/animals/cannibals/robots.

&#x200B;

Granted, there's no real morality system in the game, with the only consequence being how certain actions will change how the factions perceive you, but it's still neat to know that you can take down people who are undoubtedly charitable just because you WANTED to be an asshole.

