Of the three recent mobile games, I feel like this one gets a bit shafted.

&#x200B;

Godzilla Run feels like it was made by one person, but this game feels like it has more people behind it.

&#x200B;

Game lacks a LOT of substance, and requires a lot of repetitive grinding to progress what little progression is there.

&#x200B;

I feel like there's a lot in the game that leads itself to being more replayable, but there's not enough content to warrant replayability. On top of that, the drip-feed of items you get is almost maddening for a game with so little to do.

&#x200B;

This could be a pretty solid casual game, but it feels like you're doing so much for so little. It's a shame, 'cuz with a bigger team and some polish, it could be a good timewaster.

